{"tool_name":"slidesort","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"slidesort","home":"http://cbrc3.cbrc.jp/~shimizu/slidesort/index.php","license":"Unlicense","summary":"An algorithm that finds all similar pairs from a string pool in terms of edit distance.","addition_date":"2017-01-13T13:16:31Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:04:34.760433Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:slidesort","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"shimizu.kana@waseda.jp","name":"Kana Shimizu","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://cbrc3.cbrc.jp/~shimizu/slidesort/index.php?Usage"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-EE"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0291"},{"term":"Sequence word comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0288"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"SlideSort","operating_system":["Linux","Windows"],"owner":"seqwiki_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btq677","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Recent progress in DNA sequencing technologies calls for fast and accurate algorithms that can evaluate sequence similarity for a huge amount of short reads. Searching similar pairs from a string pool is a fundamental process of de novo genome assembly, genome-wide alignment and other important analyses. Results: In this study, we designed and implemented an exact algorithm SlideSort that finds all similar pairs from a string pool in terms of edit distance. Using an efficient pattern growth algorithm, SlideSort discovers chains of common k-mers to narrow down the search. Compared to existing methods based on single k-mers, our method is more effective in reducing the number of edit distance calculations. In comparison to backtracking methods such as BWA, our method is much faster in finding remote matches, scaling easily to tens of millions of sequences. Our software has an additional function of single link clustering, which is useful in summarizing short reads for further processing. \u00a9 The Author(s) 2010. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Shimizu K."},{"name":"Tsuda K."}],"citationCount":18,"date":"2011-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Slidesort: All pairs similarity search for short reads"},"pmcid":"PMC3035798","pmid":"21148542"}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SlideSort","home":"https://bio.tools/slidesort","license":"Unlicense","summary":"An algorithm that finds all similar pairs from a string pool in terms of edit distance.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:slidesort/app/www.cbrc.jp","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":9,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2019"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2025"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2018"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btq677","pmcid":"PMC3035798","pmid":"21148542","ref_count":12,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1985"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2006"},{"count":2,"year":"2008"},{"count":7,"year":"2009"}],"title":"SlideSort: all pairs similarity search for short reads.","year":2010}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":408,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://www.cbrc.jp/~shimizu/slidesort/"}],"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bs